  "candidate_policy_question": {
    "id": "REVIEW-GPU-BUFFER-MAP-USAGE-COMBINATION-95E",
    "status": "conditional newly assessed source/native API contract; uniqueness and owner policy for central reconciliation",
    "condition": "A caller of the public builder combines a storage use with HostRead, for example by composing storage() with with_usage(HostRead), and allocates it on a device without MAPPABLE_PRIMARY_BUFFERS. No such actual application call was established.",
    "trace": "Storage contributes STORAGE|COPY_SRC|COPY_DST; HostRead adds MAP_READ and with_usage unions them without feature-aware validation. Buffer::new rejects zero length then forwards the definition to native create_buffer and returns the wrapper if control returns. wgpu-types 29.0.4 documents that absent MAPPABLE_PRIMARY_BUFFERS, MAP_READ may be combined only with COPY_DST. The current owned-device descriptor requests only the three enumerated optional features and omits that capability. Borrowed devices may differ.",
    "implication": "The constructed descriptor is outside that documented native usage contract under the stated condition; the builder has not rejected it before the native boundary. Exact native validation/error observation, runtime outcome, ordinary caller reachability and whether this low-level API promises local rejection rather than deliberately delegating it remain unestablished.",
    "historical_relationship": "RIG-ADMISSION03-ADDITIONAL-087 explicitly observed arbitrary usage combinations being delegated to native validation. This refines that historical observation with the exact locked API and current owned-device requested feature set; do not count it as distinct until central reconciliation decides policy and overlap. It is separate from the existing copy-alignment, wrapper metadata, and uniform-packer contracts.",
    "future_repair_direction": "If the owning API contract requires admitted usage sets, validate feature-dependent combinations before native allocation or explicitly retain an appropriate validated capability/device owner; alternatively document delegated native validation if that is the intended contract. Preserve storage copy capabilities and supported mapped-only cases. Future validation is deferred.",
