  "open_questions": [
    "Is BufferDefinition deliberately a thin native descriptor builder, or should Buffer::new return a typed error for unsupported feature-dependent usage sets? Which actual callers, borrowed devices and platforms exercise those combinations?",
    "Which shader shapes, multiple uniform buffers, sparse groups, image arrays, multisampling, storage access and sampler classes are supported product contracts? Earlier validation may reject before a selected downstream operation.",
    "Do real callers mutate public shader/pipeline/buffer fields, share caches across devices, or require stronger source/module/context coherence?",
    "Which error causes or structured reasons must survive each distinct shader and pipeline boundary? Can the repeated Naga validate/unwrap be removed in a future repair without altering diagnostics?",
    "Existing F058 concerns a separate fast writer and its exact current producer/shape policy; this packet does not read or execute that writer.",
    "The claimed connected TEAM004 verify filename was an exploratory guess and is absent from extraction and transport manifest; no source has established that such a verification file existed. The actual root adoption and delegated read receipt are preserved.",
    "All support unread complements are recorded; no whole GPU crate, WGSL package, native backend, full thirteen-lens, or checkpoint3821 clearance."
